      "id": "lem-a-degreewise-split-exact-complex-with-compatible-splittings-is-contractible",
      "location": "Proof 2.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "Step 1.1 defines s_{n-1}=phi_n^{-1}j_2 pi_1 phi_{n-1} and obtains d_n s_{n-1}=i_{n-1}pi_1 phi_{n-1}. Step 2.1 then asserts that this term is phi_{n-1}^{-1}j_1 pi_1 phi_{n-1}, but the stated hypotheses require only d_n=i_{n-1}pi_2 phi_n; they do not require phi_{n-1}i_{n-1}=j_1. For the two-term identity complex Z -> Z, take phi_1=1 and phi_0=-1. All displayed hypotheses hold, but the prescribed s_0=-1 gives d_1s_0=-1, not 1_{C_0}. Thus the displayed identity in step 2.1 is false under the stated assumptions.",
